# Cloudflare Pages response headers.
#
# This site is deliberately public, so unlike the internal copy there is no Access gate behind
# these. They are what stops a demo of a hiring assessment turning up in search results, which
# would be a problem for the test itself: the questions are meant to be unseen before a candidate
# opens them.

# The CSP is worth having precisely because this deployment is public. Everything the pages need
# is served from this origin, so `default-src 'none'` with a short allowlist costs nothing and
# takes third-party script injection and form exfiltration off the table. 'unsafe-inline' is
# required by the inline <script> and <style> in admin.html and by the inline style attributes
# app.js sets on the progress bar; it is not load-bearing anywhere else. The one external
# destination, the Google Sheet in the brief, is an ordinary link and is unaffected.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; connect-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data:; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow, noarchive
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  Cache-Control: no-store
